Subject: Enter compiled functions directly from interpreter calls, and fix the inline array bounds

What this does
  Lets the register interpreter's call and method-call handlers run a callee
  that has a compiled body on a light frame, through `qjs_aot_call_light`,
  instead of `JS_CallInternal`. Corrects the element-count offset the compiled
  unit's inline array accesses use, and adds the `holey` flag's byte and mask
  to the generator layout.

Why we need it
  Binding a compiled body clears the callee's light-call flags, so every call
  into it from interpreted code took `JS_CallInternal`, `js_regvm_execute` and
  the compiled entry. Measured on a 5M-call loop, that was 256 ms against 131 ms
  for the same calls interpreted: compiling a small function made calling it
  twice as slow. With the direct entry it is 150 ms.

  The layout's `off_object_array_count` was `u.array.u1.size`, the allocated
  capacity, not the element count. An inline read or store bounded by it
  reached slots past the array's end: an append leaves the capacity above the
  count, and those slots are uninitialized.

What it adds
  regvm_t_call_aot, regvm_t_call_method_aot
                            - the call handlers' path for a light-eligible
                              callee with a compiled body; a refused entry or a
                              nearly full C stack takes the slow call
  JSAotGenLayout            - `off_object_array_count` is the element count;
                              new `off_object_holey_byte`, `object_holey_mask`

Bytecode version
  No.

diff --git a/quickjs-aot-rt.h b/quickjs-aot-rt.h
--- a/quickjs-aot-rt.h
+++ b/quickjs-aot-rt.h
@@ -98,6 +98,10 @@
     /* The per-site polymorphic property cache: where the bytecode's allocation
        is, the stride between sites, and the ways per site. */
     uint32_t off_fnbc_aot_poly, off_fnbc_aot_poly_sites, aot_poly_ways;
+    /* The byte and mask of `holey`: an inline array access refuses a holey
+       array, as the engine's own fast store does, since filling a hole has
+       bookkeeping the inline path does not do. */
+    uint32_t off_object_holey_byte, object_holey_mask;
 } JSAotGenLayout;
 
